                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Asteroid Girl is a Shoot 'Em Up game.\n\nWhere to begin... let's cut to the real reason you should avoid this game: the controls. Whether you're using a keyboard or a controller, no matter how you try to approach moving in this game, you move at least 100 pixels with every input. So imagine you're trying to dodge a projectile that will hit you head on... you move downward ever so slightly and little Asteroid Girl goes slamming into the other projectiles much further under your character.\n\nNow it wouldn't be so bad if the game had any continue system, but after 4 hits, you are dead. The game has 4 levels with 4 bosses. If you dare getting hit even once, your weapon resets to level 1 and you can barely clear the insane onslaught of enemies on the screen until you loot 2 weapon upgrades again, which if you don't have any firepower to begin with... will most likely kill you. Monsters can shoot straight at you, in diagonal and backwards, so if you keep more than 1 or 2 monsters alive, you're asking for a random bullet to kill you. Between your bullets and the enemies, it gets super confusing which are which.\n\nOh and did I mention that when you finally die, you restart from the BEGINNING? That's right, there's no saves, no checkpoints, nothing. As a reward for finishing the game, when you submit your highscore at the end, your game simply crashes! The graphics are basic, the sound effects are too and the music is super repetitive. The game is around 10 minutes long.\n\nOverall, I wouldn't recommend this to anyone, including Shoot 'Em Up enthusiasts!",
